            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aspects of cardiovascular disease in the patient infected with HIV that are of particular relevance to the emergency physician, including coronary artery disease and acute coronary syndromes, pericardial disease, and dilated cardiomyopathy are discussed in this review.</AbstractText>
